[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. Its own table shows more than that.
The reports were merged on their subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)),
and a subject says *that* a date is wrong, not *how*. This page splits #4471 by what each report
shows, and files one ticket per problem.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix closes the <code>parser</code> ticket only. Reports for <code>hint</code> and
<code>one-day</code> keep coming after it ships.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

### `parser`: day-first dates are read month first

It covers <ProblemCount ticket={4471} problem="parser" /> reports. The shared parser reads every date month
first, and every tenant on file writes the day first. A booking for 7 April (07/04) goes out as
4 July. It reaches every tenant, through the app, by email and through the form. This is the bug
the queued fix is for. Ticket: [#1](https://github.com/mdubel/mega-dev/issues/1).

### `hint`: booking-v3 tells day-first tenants to type the month first

It covers <ProblemCount ticket={4471} problem="hint" /> reports. `booking-v3` prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its
date field. Its tenants' people type what it says, month first, and the form reads the date the
tenant's way, day first. The date swaps in the form, before the parser sees it. The symptom is the
same as `parser`, so a subject can't tell them apart; the fix is different. Ticket: [#2](https://github.com/mdubel/mega-dev/issues/2).

### `one-day`: the date moves by one day

It covers <ProblemCount ticket={4471} problem="one-day" /> reports. Day and month stay in place; the date
moves by a day. One meeting showed on Tuesday in Lisbon and on Monday in Toronto, so the date
crosses a time zone somewhere. The desk read these in the queue and noted them; #4471 still counts
them under `parser`, in a footnote. The parser fix won't change them. Ticket: [#3](https://github.com/mdubel/mega-dev/issues/3).

## How this was counted

- **One report per id.** The ticket system exports pages that overlap, so some reports come twice.
- **Cause from the tenant, not from intake.** `causeOf` in `causes.ts` places a report by its
  tenant's locale and booking form. Intake's tag follows the reporter's browser: it tags every
  `en-US` browser as `hint`, wherever the tenant is.
- **What a report says beats where it was filed.** A report whose text shows a one-day move
  (`desk-notes.json`) is its own problem, not a footnote under `parser`.
- **A report with no date in it** stays with its tenant's cause.

Every number on this page is computed from the export when the page is built. When the desk adds
reports or notes, the table follows.

## For the desk

- Merging on subject alone put every one of these problems in one ticket. The same subject lines
  turn up under each of them. Decision 0001 is accepted, so it isn't edited here: it needs a new
  record that replaces it.
- When a report doesn't match its ticket's symptom, split it out; a footnote keeps it on the
  wrong fix.

